      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the **Guarded Write Journal** works as a transaction mechanism for the guarded tool executor.\n\nKey points:\n\n- **Prior state recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s previous state in an in-memory write journal\u2014either the previous content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal rolls back every recorded write in reverse order\u2014restoring previous content or deleting newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This provides transaction-like behavior without needing an external database, since the journal itself serves as the transaction log held in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\n- **Query agent note**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the journal\u0027s rollback functionality since it has no write capability.",
